WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.630
What does justice really mean?

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:06.580
Do those in law enforcement have a responsibility
to behave more ethically than the average

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.580
citizen?

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.260
These are the big questions at the forefront
of the latest psychological thriller making

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.179
waves on HBO Max - The Little Things.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:18.960
The film stars a trio of Academy Award winners
as deputy sheriff Joe Deacon, played by Denzel

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.570
Washington, gets wrapped up in a Los Angeles
crime investigation with detective Jimmy Baxter,

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.540
played by Rami Malek , taking the lead.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.859
There's a serial killer on the loose, and
both men obsess over figuring out who's behind

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:32.230
these deadly attacks.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.310
Their search brings them to an outcast by
the name of Albert Sparma, played by Jared

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.110
Leto , who seems to fit the profile, but when
it comes to solving a case as messy as this

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.220
one, not everything is as it seems.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.280
The Little Things is one of the first movies
subject to the bold new release strategy from

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.760
Warner Bros. that sees films debuting simultaneously
in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.250
The radical distribution plan is designed
to sidestep issues created by the ongoing

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.900
COVID-19 pandemic.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.610
As such, there's a lot riding on the film's
success.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.400
Even though we may not have any official numbers
on how well the film has done on the streaming

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.110
platform as of this video, it seems to have
caught on with audiences.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.790
Don't worry - we won't spoil the ending for
you here.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.530
"No, don't say anything, no spoilers!"

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.500
The response from professional critics has
been decidedly mixed on The Little Things,

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.690
according to Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:24.150
So far, it's garnered a 48% critical score,
which is a bit shy of fresh, but it's doing

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.500
a lot better when you look at what general
audiences have to say.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.540
By audience metrics, it has a rating of 64%
with over 250 reviews accumulated.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.950
The general consensus among audience members
is that the three leads — Washington, Malek,

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.770
and Leto — are phenomenal in this film,
and really give it their all.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.900
One of the verified audience reviews praises
Leto's work in this:

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.180
"The acting was fantastic.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.420
I never [thought] Jared Leto could be this
creepy!!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.020
It had some really suspenseful moments."

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.240
Leto has stated that he drew inspiration for
this role from a surprising world leader:

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.670
North Korean dictator Kim Jong-un.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.370
The results are suitably creepy and entertaining.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.920
As any good psychological thriller should,
The Little Things has a way of burrowing into

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.700
your mind and making you rethink everything
you've seen in the film.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.069
One reviewer by the name of Farlisa writes,

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:14.280
"This is a mind twisted movie.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.650
My husband and I are still replaying the events
in our heads."

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.160
With other comments like, quote, "Movie is
a must see" and "Unexpected ending but still

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.750
exciting and worth the watch," it's clear
this film, while perhaps divisive, is likely

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.840
worth a watch if you're a fan of thrillers.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.380
In the event you're still on the fence about
whether or not to give The Little Things a

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.319
chance, then perhaps it's prudent to compare
it to a different thriller held in high regard

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:37.319
— Seven.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:42.600
The 1995 neo-noir starring Morgan Freeman,
Brad Pitt, and Gwyneth Paltrow is one of director

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.210
David Fincher's best films, both due to the
moody atmosphere it creates as well as the

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:50.051
shocking ending that still terrifies audiences
to this day.

00:02:50.051 --> 00:02:55.160
A lot of people over on Twitter are comparing
the classic 90s film with The Little Things

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.430
with @Gameoverluke writing,

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:59.040
"If you liked Seven then watch The Little
Things!

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.489
Such a good movie."

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:04.470
Regardless of people's opinions on the film
overall, one thing is clear — people love

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.069
Denzel Washington in this, and pretty much
any other movie he's in.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:12.239
After all, it's not a coincidence that you
see comments like "Denzel is the best actor

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:17.030
of my time" and "Denzel Washington is still
the GOAT" among the fan reviews.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.910
As with any movie, it's best to watch it for
yourself to form your own opinion.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.720
You can check it out on HBO Max until the
end of February.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.300
If one thing's clear from all of this, it's
that you don't want to be left out of the

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.350
conversation.

